#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166927 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c444e892-e49f-5ea7-9ac9-c51078566c40" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Equilibrium Points of the Modified Lotka-Volterra System"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0cca672-22d2-56b4-8615-61d6e24b7f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0cca672-22d2-56b4-8615-61d6e24b7f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370418} :answer-field/id #uuid "07b070e5-7be6-50e8-a4a0-beb9ca54ef6f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370417} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dda70e62-0307-5f61-be89-38a5799d0f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda70e62-0307-5f61-be89-38a5799d0f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370420} :answer-field/id #uuid "793a6dcc-2165-52e4-94f6-60749fcac9b0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370419} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3512a5da-77e9-5ff0-a44a-28af35917f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3512a5da-77e9-5ff0-a44a-28af35917f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370422} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1e028e8-2b52-5edb-aa50-089cf299893a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6734dc20-5e4c-5ba3-a922-996f26cded96" :question/math-academy-id "q-335607" :question/problem "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=4x(1-0.25x)-2xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-6y+3xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x(1-0.25x)-2xy=0 \\\\ -6y+3xy=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6y+3xy & =0 \\\\ y(-6+3x) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $y=0$ or $x=2.$ We consider both cases separately.\n\n- If $y=0,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x(1-0.25x)-2x(0) & =0 \\\\ 4x(0.25x-1) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,\\,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the first two equilibria are $(0,0)$ and $(4,0).$\n\n- If $x=2,$ substituting it into the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)(1-0.25(2))-2(2)y & =0 \\\\ 4-4y & =0 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, another equilibrium is $(2,1).$\n\nTherefore, the equilibria of the model are\n\n$$\n(0,0),\\,(4,0),\\,(2,1).\n$$"}]}
